        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Arthur White, David Jason, John Sullivan, Derek Trotter, Denzil Tulser, Ernie Trigg\n- Works: A Touch of Frost, Only Fools and Horses\n- Roles: stage and screen actor, police archivist\n\nFacts:\n- Arthur White was born in December 1933 and is an English stage and screen actor.\n- Arthur White is known for occasionally playing police archivist Ernie Trigg in the crime drama A Touch of Frost.\n- Arthur White appeared in A Touch of Frost alongside his real-life younger brother David Jason.\n- David Jason is best known for portraying Derek Trotter, known by the nickname Del Boy, in the British television series Only Fools and Horses.\n- John Sullivan wrote the British television series Only Fools and Horses.\n- In Only Fools and Horses, Denzil Tulser is a good friend of Del Boy.",
